# VIGIL off-HOST backup push — environment file (copy to ~/.config/vigil/backup-push.env, chmod 600)
# =====================================================================
# Read by vigil-backup-push.service. Three settings:
#
#   VIGIL_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE — the ONLY key to the encrypted backups. Read from the
#       ENVIRONMENT by both legs, NEVER passed on the command line, NEVER stored
#       inside the backup — lose it and the backups are UNRECOVERABLE by design.
#       The push transports CIPHERTEXT ONLY; this passphrase never leaves the host.
#
#   VIGIL_BASE_DIR — the offense engine home to back up (default .vigil-live,
#       relative to WorkingDirectory=%h/vigil). Give an ABSOLUTE path if elsewhere.
#
#   VIGIL_PUSH_DEST — where to replicate the ENCRYPTED files. Only the LOCAL-DIRECTORY
#       transport ships today, so this is a path (or local:<path>):
#         * a mounted remote filesystem   e.g. /mnt/backup-nfs/vigil
#         * an sshfs mount                e.g. /home/you/mnt/remote-vigil
#         * a removable disk              e.g. /media/you/backup-usb/vigil
#       rsync://, scp://, and s3:// are recognised but NOT built yet — they error
#       clearly with the contract to implement (tools/backup/transport.py).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HONEST WARNING — this unit needs the NETWORK and an at-rest passphrase.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# vigil-backup-push.service runs WITH the network (PrivateNetwork=no) so it can
# reach the remote; the routine vigil-backup.service stays air-gapped. A passphrase
# in a 0600 env file is weaker than typing it interactively — see the notes in
# vigil-backup.env.example (systemd-credentials is the stronger alternative). The
# transported bytes are already encrypted, but WHO CAN READ the remote directory is
# the operator's responsibility — lock it down, and test a restore FROM the pushed copy.

VIGIL_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=change-me-to-a-long-random-passphrase
VIGIL_BASE_DIR=.vigil-live
VIGIL_PUSH_DEST=/mnt/backup-remote/vigil
